# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc atanh, atan. atanh(z) = ln((1+z)/(1-z))/2 and atan's ln((i+z)/(i-z)) take the ln of 1+O(z), so for a small non-real z (exact or a complex MPFR value) the evalf cancels -log10|z| digits in both parts and a part far below the other is lost: at Digits 40 evalf(atanh(i/10^1000)) = -0.5e-2000*i (right 1e-1000*i), atanh(10^-1000*(1+i)) the same (right 1e-1000+1e-1000*i), evalf(atan(i/10^1000)) = 0 (right 1e-1000*i); the exact atanh(10^-100*i) was ln((10^200-1+2*10^100*i)/(10^200+1))/2, which cancels the same way. Now a complex MPFR z (parts MPFR or exactly 0, the larger below 1/4) is computed by its parts, s = |z|^2: atanh(z) = atanh(2x/(1+s))/2 + i*atan(2y/(1-s))/2, atan(z) = atan(2x/(1-s))/2 + i*atanh(2y/(1+s))/2, MPFR's real atanh and atan; an exact non-real z below 1/4 (its double; a part that reads 0 too) gives atanh(i*y) = i*atan(y) for a zero real part (radians), else atanh stays unevaluated, as for a real x (patch 0027). Larger z, doubles and free names keep their forms (atanh(i/2) = ln((3+4*i)/5)/2).
